    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20260930-1302-the-loop-s-fence-blocked-the-read-only-g","brief":"B20260930-0929-vloop-close-export-workspace.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"partly","by":"assistant","occurred":"2026-09-30","recorded":"2026-09-30T16:54:00Z","backfilled":true,"summary":"the loop's fence blocked the read-only git remote -v","trigger":"permission denials in the session records","done":"denied only the git remote subcommands that change something","automation":"reading the denials is automatable; judging a rule too broad is partly","context":"B4's session records showed the planner denied `git remote -v`: the fence's `Bash(git remote:*)` prefix also blocked the read-only form. Narrowed to the mutating subcommands (commit 48dd7ef); the loop suite stayed 47/47.","suggested":"deny only the mutating git remote subcommands.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"the operator: 'go ahead!'."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/052/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20260930-1305-schema-files-counted-as-other-lines","brief":"B20260930-0929-vloop-close-export-workspace.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"yes","by":"assistant","occurred":"2026-09-30","recorded":"2026-09-30T16:54:00Z","backfilled":true,"summary":"schema files counted as 'other' lines","trigger":"the by-task table in the rehearsed run record","done":"classified schemas/** as code in the repo config","automation":"a check for unclassified lines above a threshold","context":"The rehearsed B4 run record showed T1 with 110 'other' lines: the schema .json files, unclassified. `metrics.code` gained `schemas/**` in this repo's config (commit 1fc8e15).","suggested":"classify schemas/** as code.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"the operator: 'go ahead!'."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/053/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20261001-1005-plan-md-run-id-wording","brief":"B20261001-0723-vloop-run-driver.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"partly","by":"assistant","occurred":"2026-10-01","recorded":"2026-10-01T09:13:20Z","summary":"the updated domain plan.md said the driver stamps run_id as the brief's name","trigger":"reading the docs the run changed, then checking the run id vloop actually wrote","done":"fixed the line; recorded through close --finding","automation":"a test comparing the domain's identifier table with the code's run id; the docs-vs-binary pass planned for B8","context":"Verifying B6: docs/domain/execution/plan.md, updated by the run, said the driver stamps run_id as 'the brief's name'. The driver wrote 'B20260101-0900-a' (the run id) in a hand-run check. Fixed the line; recorded through `close --finding`, its first real use.","suggested":"fix the line and record it with close --finding.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"the operator: 'go ahead, finish B6'."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/054/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20261001-1338-eval-cases-fail-to-load-setup-key","brief":"B20261001-1025-vloop-skills.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"yes","by":"assistant","occurred":"2026-10-01","recorded":"2026-10-01T12:38:50Z","summary":"all 13 eval cases fail to load: their prompt.md declares setup, which the eval tool does not know","trigger":"Before running the full eval suite (up to $40), a single-case probe with --runs 1 --ablation none --max-cost-usd 1.","done":"","automation":"A structural check that loads every case with the eval tool's own loader (or its key list), and a planner rule: a brief that names an external format pins its exact keys from the tool, not from memory.","context":"B7's T8 wrote the 13 cases as prompt.md with 'setup: scaffold.sh'. claude plugin eval rejected every one ('unknown frontmatter key \"setup\"', allowed: schema_version, name, description, tags, plugins, runs, expected_outcome, model, max_turns, timeout_seconds, allowed_tools, artifact_publish, growthbook_overrides, append_system_prompt, env); scaffold_script lives in the case.yaml format. B7's brief said cases plant repos 'with a scaffold script' without pinning the format, and its structural check only required max_turns and allowed_tools. Nothing ran; $0 spent. Recorded as defect D20261001-1338.","suggested":"Probe one case before the whole suite; then convert the cases to the format that supports a scaffold, and make the structural check reject keys the tool does not know.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"Pending: the fix is proposed to the operator."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/055/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20261001-2310-eval-suite-first-run","brief":"B20261001-1025-vloop-skills.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"partly","by":"both","occurred":"2026-10-01","recorded":"2026-10-01T22:10:00Z","summary":"the full eval suite's first run: every review case caught, the plan and work cases held back by the sandbox","trigger":"The operator approved the full suite at a $40 ceiling after the probe passed.","done":"","automation":"The eval tool reporting denied tool calls per run; a pre-flight case that runs `git status` and a compound command in the sandbox.","context":"13 cases × 3 runs × 2 arms, `-j 2`, model claude-opus-5-5 (the calibration's baseline was sonnet): $17.97, 25 minutes, overall 0.89, mean delta over no plugin 0.85. Review: all nine cases FAIL the planted work in 27 of 27 runs and name the defect (`06` included); two runs (05, 07) lost only `verdict-validates`. The without-plugin arm scores 0 everywhere but `work-disputes-impossible-gate` (0.5). Plan and work: `plan-valid-state` 0.5 (never validated), `plan-checks-its-gates` 0.41, `language-es` 0.85, `work-disputes-impossible-gate` 0.92; nearly every loss is a `*-validates` grader or a judge reading a transcript in which no gate ran. Two environment causes, read from the report: (1) git cannot run in the sandbox: `/usr/bin/git` is the xcrun stub, whose cache write to `$TMPDIR` is denied, though Homebrew's git is first on the operator's PATH; (2) sessions run in don't-ask mode and use compound commands (`cat …; echo ---; git ls-files`) whose unrelated segments (`echo`, `ls`, `find`, `which`) are not granted, so they are denied, and after a few denials a session stops using Bash, `vloop schema validate` included. The run transcripts were not kept (no `--keep-temp`).","suggested":"One diagnostic run of `plan-valid-state` with `--keep-temp` (about $0.5) to read the trace's PATH and every denial, then fix in the environment (a real git first on the sessions' PATH) and the cases (grant the read-only commands sessions reach for), and re-run only the plan and work cases.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"The operator approved the diagnostic run (2026-10-02): `plan-valid-state`, 1 run, no baseline, `--keep-temp`, $0.37, score 0.50 (the same two `*-validates` graders lost). The trace: the session's first Bash call was one compound command (`cat …; echo ----; cat CLAUDE.md; echo ----; git ls-files; git rev-parse HEAD; vloop config get shell; echo \"areas=[$(vloop config get areas)]\"`); don't-ask mode denied it whole with a message that reads as \"Bash is denied\", and the session never tried Bash again. A Grep outside its working directory (into the plugin's source) was denied too. It read the repo with Read and Glob, wrote `state.json`, and said it could not check it. Git was never reached, so the xcrun-stub cause is neither confirmed nor ruled out. The production driver runs sessions with `--permission-mode auto` under the fence, whose allow list is wider (`ls`, `head`, `tail`, `find`, `wc`, `jq`, `git show`, `vloop task validate`, `vloop task gate`); the cases grant a narrower set in don't-ask mode, so the evals are stricter than a real run. The operator approved the fix and a rerun: every case now grants the fence's allow list plus `echo`, `git ls-files`, `grep`, `sh`, `chmod`, `test`, `vloop task`, held by `TestEvalGrantsCoverFence` (17f260e). Rerun of the four plan and work cases, 3 runs × 2 arms, $6.94: `plan-valid-state` 0.50, `plan-checks-its-gates` 0.33, `language-es` 0.78, `work-disputes-impossible-gate` 0.92 — no better. Single commands now run; compound ones (`for` loops, `$(…)`, `;` chains with ungranted parts) are still denied. The traces show two causes underneath: (1) the sessions run a stale `vloop` (`~/go/bin/vloop`, built 2026-09-29: `unknown command \"schema\"`, `\"task\"`, `\"status\"`, `unknown config key \"shell\"`) — the sandbox denies reads under `/private/tmp` and `/Users`, allowing back only a few bin directories (`~/go/bin`, `~/.local/bin`, nvm's), so the freshly built binary first on PATH in the scratchpad is unreadable and the old one wins; (2) git is the xcrun stub (`git: error: couldn't create cache file`). The first suite's validation losses, review cases included, have the same causes. The operator approved `go install ./cmd/vloop` (replacing the stale `~/go/bin/vloop`) and a probe: `plan-valid-state`, 1 run, no baseline, $0.40, score 0.80 — `state-validates` and `task-validate` pass. Two environment causes remain, both in the trace: the sessions inherit the operator's `TMPDIR` (`/var/folders/…/T`), which the sandbox denies, so the gate's `mktemp -d` fails; and `git` resolves to the xcrun stub `/usr/bin/git`, which cannot write its cache there and finds no Command Line Tools (`xcode-select: Failed to locate 'git'`), though Homebrew's git is first on the operator's PATH. The one grader lost, `plan-quality` (judge 0/3), reads a sound plan: its \"no absolute path anywhere\" clause is met literally by `#!/bin/sh` in an acceptance criterion and `cd /` in the verify — a grader wording defect, not the plan's. Three throwaway probe cases in a scratch copy of the plugin (haiku, about $0.13 in all) showed the real causes. The Command Line Tools are installed; `DEVELOPER_DIR` does not help the stub. Inside the eval sandbox `$PATH` lists `/opt/homebrew/bin` before `/usr/bin`, yet the shell resolves bare `git` to `/usr/bin/git` (`type -a git` lists only it, after `hash -r` too), and the stub fails because it writes its cache to macOS's per-user temp directory (`/var/folders/…/T`), which the sandbox denies whatever `TMPDIR` says. `env git`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/git` and `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git` all work. `TMPDIR` is already a writable sandbox directory, but macOS `mktemp -d` without a template ignores it and uses the same denied directory, so a gate written with `mktemp -d` fails in the evals though it works in a real run. The operator approved four fixes: a `git` wrapper script at `~/.local/bin/git` (written by the operator; the assistant's write outside the repo was refused by the permission check), the plan skill's `mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gate.XXXXXX\"` rule and the `plan-quality` rewording (4e643af), and a rerun. A probe confirmed bare `git` and the templated `mktemp` work in the sandbox. Rerun, 3 runs × 2 arms, $6.80: `plan-valid-state` 1.00 (was 0.50), `work-disputes-impossible-gate` 0.98 (0.92), `language-es` 0.78 (0.85; `prose-in-spanish` lost 2 of 3 on a plan whose prose reads as Spanish, with loanwords such as test, brief, flag and shell), `plan-checks-its-gates` 0.44 (0.41). In the last, the planner ran `vloop task gate` and its gate failed on the base for the right reason, but its fixture checks in a scratch directory (a heredoc, `$(…)`, `mktemp`) were denied: don't-ask mode denied each command with a parameter expansion, a `$(…)` or a heredoc into a file, though every command in it was granted, which auto mode in a real run would allow. `ran-the-gates-on-the-base` also assumes the first draft's gate passed on the base. The pre-flight is now `tools/eval-preflight/` and docs/guide/evals.md (a10e60c). The operator chose to fix the graders: `prose-in-spanish` accepts technical loanwords and `ran-the-gates-on-the-base` judges each gate's last run (662acd0); rerun $3.93: `language-es` 1.00 in 3 of 3, `plan-checks-its-gates` 0.22, its two haiku judges failing transcripts that show `gate T1: fail (exit 1, …)`. Both gate graders became regex on vloop's gate output — `gate T\u003cn\u003e: fail (exit` must appear, `gate T\u003cn\u003e: pass (` must not (96c60bf); rerun $1.87: 0.67 in 3 of 3, the only loss `fixture-read-back`, whose fixture checks don't-ask mode denies. The without-plugin arm scores 0.33, `no-gate-passes-on-the-base` passing vacuously where no gate ran. Final for the plan and work cases: `plan-valid-state` 1.00, `work-disputes-impossible-gate` 0.98, `language-es` 1.00, `plan-checks-its-gates` 0.67 (a known limit of the eval sandbox). Eval spend across 2026-10-02: about $20.70."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/056/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20261002-1426-b7-s-acceptance-run-restarted-detached-t","brief":"B20261001-1025-vloop-skills.loop-brief","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"partly","by":"both","occurred":"2026-10-02","recorded":"2026-10-02T13:26:10Z","summary":"B7's acceptance run: restarted detached, then verified by hand","trigger":"The operator approved the url-shortener acceptance run at a $40 ceiling","done":"Set up in ~/source/personal/url-shortener-vloop-acceptance (the sample at 9a197a7, shell loop and its CLAUDE.md block removed, vloop init --stacks typescript, the brief converted with its body unchanged, the folder trusted by the operator). The first start ran as a session background task capped at 2 hours; it was stopped in planning, its branch, run folder and .running lock removed, and restarted detached with nohup. Result: complete, 10/10 first-pass in 10 iterations, $4.21 (plan $1.98 opus; work $1.39 and review $0.84 sonnet), against the shell loop's 10/10 in 11 iterations, 1 rejection, about $19.86. Every record validates (state, 21 sessions, 20 reports, 10 iterations, metrics); every task has a kind. On a fresh clone: npm ci, 3 unit and 26 e2e tests pass, the build boots, the committed smoke script passes, and the brief's worked example holds over HTTP. Wall time 105 min against 23 min of sessions: the Mac idle-slept at 12:43 and advanced only in maintenance wakes until 14:22. Metrics undercount tests: D20261002-1425.","automation":"vloop run holding a no-idle-sleep assertion on macOS (caffeinate -i) for the run's duration; a run that cannot outlive the operator's session started detached by default","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":""},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/057/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20261002-2118-the-url-shortener-benchmark-the-cost-dro","brief":"","phase":"verify","kind":"verification-finding","automatable":"partly","by":"both","occurred":"2026-10-02","recorded":"2026-10-02T20:18:58Z","summary":"the url-shortener benchmark: the cost drop is the models; vloop's planner costs twice the shell loop's","trigger":"The operator asked whether vloop's lower cost in B7's acceptance run came from the model change, the skills being largely the same","done":"The shell loop rerun on the new models in ~/source/personal/url-shortener-shell-rerun (9a197a7, defaults: opus and sonnet aliases, $40, 30 iterations), detached under caffeinate -i. Original 2026-08-18 (opus 5, sonnet 5): 10/10, 11 iterations, 1 rejection, $19.87, turns plan 41 / work 327 / review 196, 27 permission denials. Rerun 2026-10-02 (opus 5.5, sonnet 5.5): 11/11, 12 iterations, 0 rejections, 1 gate failure, $3.34 (plan $1.01, work $1.50, review $0.83), turns 12 / 78 / 55, 2 denials. vloop the same day and models: 10/10, 10 iterations, $4.21 (plan $1.98, work $1.39, review $0.84), turns 27 / 82 / 50, 0 denials. Both apps verified on a fresh clone: npm ci, unit and e2e tests, boot, the worked example over HTTP. The models explain the drop (about 6x); work and review match across drivers; vloop's planner costs about 2x, plausibly its gate checks on the base. One pair of runs.","automation":"a benchmark command that runs a fixed brief under both drivers or two model sets and tabulates turns, cost and outcome per phase","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":""},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/058/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
    intervention_test.go:81: {"schema":"intervention/v2","id":"I20260929-2325-the-bsd-tools-lesson-into-later-briefs","brief":"B20260929-2148-vloop-state-tasks-status.loop-brief","phase":"close","kind":"carry-forward","automatable":"partly","by":"assistant","occurred":"2026-09-29","recorded":"2026-09-30T16:54:00Z","backfilled":true,"summary":"the BSD-tools lesson into later briefs","trigger":"B2's stall","done":"written into B3's and B4's constraints, then into the operator skill","automation":"a lessons store the next brief's design step reads","context":"After B2's stall on (|/), the constraint 'Gates run on macOS with its BSD tools' was written into B3's and B4's briefs, then into the operator skill's lessons.","suggested":"carry the lesson into every later brief.","options":[],"recommended":{"option":0,"why":""},"decided":{"option":0,"adjusted":false,"text":"the assistant, within the operator skill's remit; no operator decision asked."},"agreement":"no-options"}: /var/folders/ws/6myjg51x6cl_gc8w8v3726080000gn/T/TestExistingInterventionsValidate2977100304/059/i.json: /schema: value must be 'intervention/v1'
